{
  "format": "spelunking-ruleset",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "b2.1",
  "note": "b1.7 + light (D051, D052) + the seismic probe (D053). Your light is a radius of base + floor(ore / orePer + loot / lootPer) tiles, counting the ore and loot in the pack, so it resets when you teleport home. It spreads from you through open cells within the radius and lights them and the rock faces bordering them, never through rock. The surface is always lit, and whatever was lit stays seen for good. ↓ on a floor (not a plank, not at a ledge edge, where it still climbs over) is the probe: you stand still while rings spread from you, one every ringTicks, and reveal everything they cross, rock interiors too, for good. A flick reaches light radius + flick rings; a hold grows on until radius + hold or until released, never ending short of the flick's reach. A tap or a new swipe doesn't cut it short, and the run ends with it (stop probe). The rest is b1.7: a flick follows the world (walks, walks up and down steps and ramps, tunnels) and stops with \"?\" where it would have to build; a hold goes in a straight line, lays planks and digs steps, pauses holdPauseTicks after each step and ends on release (D046). Every build places a plank, paid 1 rock (D038, D039); runs stop only at a wall or a plank crossing (D040, D045); clinging and gravity (D035).",
